# Nautilus AWS Lab — Troubleshoot VPC Internet Connectivity

## 1. Task Overview

The Nautilus Development Team deployed a web application on an Amazon EC2 instance running Nginx inside the `nautilus-vpc` VPC. Although the security group allowed inbound HTTP traffic on port 80, the application was initially inaccessible from the internet.

The task was to investigate the VPC configuration, restore internet connectivity, and verify that the application was accessible over HTTP.

## 2. Objectives

- Inspect the `nautilus-vpc` VPC configuration.
- Identify and repair the Internet Gateway routing issue.
- Ensure the public subnet has an active default route to the Internet Gateway.
- Verify inbound TCP port 80 in the EC2 security group.
- Confirm that the Nginx application responds to external HTTP requests.

