## 10. Conclusion

The connectivity issue was traced to the VPC's Internet Gateway routing configuration. The Internet Gateway route was restored to an active state, the security group was verified to permit HTTP traffic on port 80, and the Nginx server returned an HTTP `200 OK` response.

This task demonstrates practical AWS troubleshooting skills involving VPCs, Internet Gateways, route tables, security groups, EC2 public IP addressing, and HTTP connectivity validation.

**Final outcome:** The web application responded successfully over HTTP at `http://44.222.201.167`.

